          <declname>modName</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
The mesh buffers the fix has to put back after a remapped draw, each with the resource it is parked in:
every one the mod&apos;s shared-resource OVERRIDE list binds that its CLEANUP list does not already restore
(``vb0``, which WWMI&apos;s own pair handles). On the mod&apos;s own character each draw is matched by one of its
sections, so a buffer left bound is rebound before anything reads it; remapped, the first draw of a target
slot the mod does not cover inherits the mod&apos;s buffers. Empty for a mod without both lists
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>data</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The mod&apos;s parse data </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>sections</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The collect of every key of every <computeroutput>section</computeroutput>_ (:cpp:member:<computeroutput><ref refid="struct_a_g_remap_core_1_1_ini_parse_rows_1aacf65feec57fb8186edad9d215597abf" kindref="member">IniParseRows::Sections</ref></computeroutput>) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>overrideList</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The mod&apos;s override list (<computeroutput>CommandListOverrideSharedResources</computeroutput>) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>cleanupList</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The mod&apos;s cleanup list (<computeroutput>CommandListCleanupSharedResources</computeroutput>) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>modName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The mod the fix is for, which names the resources (<computeroutput>ResourceBypass&lt;Reg&gt;&lt;Mod&gt;RemapFix</computeroutput>) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The bypasses </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
