        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
The bypass pair&apos;s sections: an empty resource for each bypass -- a handle ``= ref &lt;reg&gt;`` parks a binding in,
like the mod&apos;s own ``[ResourceBypassVB0]`` -- and the list that binds each register back from it. The
capture before the override list rebinds a register, and the ``run =`` of the restore list at the end of
the cleanup list, are edits on the mod&apos;s own lists (a :cpp:class:`RegAnchorAdd` and a :cpp:class:`RegAdd`)
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>z3</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The Z3 context the sections are built in </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>bypasses</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The bypasses (<ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_w_w_m_i_sections_1a19be270374ab1430312e4d261f13bc10" kindref="member">bypasses</ref>) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>restoreList</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The restore list&apos;s name (<ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_w_w_m_i_sections_1a896d348b30ddb329f43fe1f8d2cd8fe8" kindref="member">restoreListName</ref>) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The sections, empty when there are no bypasses </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
